          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Kieran Hardy faces knee surgery and months out, missing Wales' autumn Tests",
          "body": "Ospreys transition coach Richard Kelly confirmed on Tuesday that Wales scrum-half Kieran Hardy needs knee surgery and faces months, not weeks, on the sidelines. The 32-cap international was helped off in the first half of Friday's 38-31 win at Dragons and had been expected to feature in head coach Steve Tandy's autumn Tests. BBC Sport says he also appears a serious doubt for next year's Six Nations, a development likely to increase calls for former Wales scrum-half Gareth Davies to reverse his retirement."
